# BA loop (product intent)

Applies when capturing or refining a **human product idea** before implementation.
Authority: @docs/agents/BA_LOOP.md (draft), @.agentic/roles/ba.primary.yaml, WI-0050.

## Prefer the implemented loop

Run the durable BA loop via `devctl`, not ad-hoc chat-only analysis:

```bash
# Open a new intent run (creates .agentic/runs/RUN-INTENT-<n>/)
devctl intent run "One-line product idea or objective"

# Resume after a blocked question (exit code 3)
devctl intent resume RUN-INTENT-1 --answer "Human answer here"

# Optional: override runtime (default resolves planning → claude-subscription)
devctl intent run "..." --runtime claude-subscription
```

Exit codes match `devctl run`: 0 parked or complete, 2 configuration error,
3 blocked on a question the human must answer.

The loop writes a run record, specialist preflight under `specialists/`, and parks
on the human-owned `product_spec` gate. PRD/ADS projection (WI-0051) is stubbed;
review `handoff/pass-*-spec-review.md` until that lands.

## Runtime note

Step 4 delegates to the **provider CLI** (`claude` or `codex` per
`.agentic/project.yaml` `runtime_preferences.planning`), not to this Cursor session.
Orchestrate from Cursor; the CLI session is the BA delegate. Requires the chosen
provider on PATH and authenticated.

## When continuing in Cursor chat

If the human is answering a blocked question or refining intent in chat instead of
`--answer`, treat the conversation as input to the loop:

1. Read the open run: `.agentic/runs/RUN-INTENT-<n>/record.yaml`
2. Synthesize specialist notes from `specialists/` — advisory only, never forward verbatim
3. Ask focused clarifying questions before any specification (at least one when ambiguity remains)
4. Use `QUESTION: ` prefix when stopping for human judgment; use `SPEC OUTLINE:` only when
   readiness criteria in BA_LOOP.md are satisfied and no open questions remain
5. Never close `product_spec` or write approval records without explicit human instruction
6. Prefer recording answers via `devctl intent resume ... --answer` so the run record stays authoritative

## Non-negotiables (BA profile)

- **Human at the top.** `product_spec` passes only on explicit human approval (ISC-10).
- **Specialists are advisory.** Compliance and legal preflight report to the BA lead; they do not speak to the human directly (ADR-005).
- **No implementation.** `ba.primary` denies `repository.write` and `shell.exec` — capture intent, do not ship code in the same session.
- **One work store.** Intent runs live under `.agentic/runs/`; product work items appear later via grooming, not parallel markdown backlogs.
